course: dictionary
lesson: 5435
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. Lamb is one of them. You can tell which meaning is meant by reading the words around it, which is called the context. «Look at the lambs in the fields» is about animals, because fields are where farm animals live.
explain: Lamb can be an animal, the meat we eat, a kind person, or a word for a sheep giving birth. «A lamb whose mother has no milk is fed by bottle» is about a baby sheep, because the mother and the milk make that clear. Ask yourself: which meaning fits here?
explain: Swap your meaning into the sentence to check it. If someone says «you're a lamb» to a child who helped tidy up, a young sheep would not make sense, so it means a gentle, kind person. Context is your clue, and a dictionary can confirm it.
fact: A lamb is a young sheep.
fact: Lamb is also the meat of a young sheep.
fact: «Like a lamb» means quietly and gently, and «you're a lamb» can mean you are a kind person.
fact: A lamb is a mammal, born in spring, and it drinks its mother's milk.
fact: A ewe is a female sheep, and «lambing season» is when sheep give birth.
exercise: «In spring, look at the lambs in the fields but keep away.» What does lambs mean here? | A type of field | Meat from a dinner plate | A gentle, kind person | *Young sheep
exercise: Mum says to a child who helped tidy up, «You're a lamb.» What does she mean? | A young sheep | Meat for dinner | *A gentle, kind person | To give birth
exercise: Which word means what a sheep does when it gives birth? | Meat | Lamb's | *To lamb | Lambs
test: Dani says, «Lamb is for tea tonight.» What does lamb mean? | A gentle, kind person | *Meat of a young sheep | A young sheep in the field | To give birth
test: «Keep dogs on a lead, because ewes panic.» What is a ewe? | *A female sheep | A dog | A field where sheep graze | A young sheep
exam: In «A lamb whose mother has no milk is fed by bottle», what does lamb mean? | To give birth | The meat of a young sheep | *A young sheep | A gentle, kind person
